course: dictionary
lesson: 12345
title: One word, three meanings: cranberry
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cranberry is a small, round, red berry that is very sour. It grows on low bushes in wet, boggy ground. «Grandma spooned cranberry sauce onto her turkey.» The word sauce tells you the cranberries have been made into something you pour over food.
explain: Words next to a word are its context, and they leave clues. «Her scarf was a deep cranberry colour.» Here cranberry is not a fruit at all. It is the deep red colour of the berries, and the word colour is the clue.
explain: Some clues come from the place or the job. «The farmer flooded the field so the berries would float.» A field full of water is a bog, so cranberry bog means the wet ground where the bushes grow.
fact: A cranberry is a small, round, red, very sour berry.
fact: Cranberries grow on low bushes in wet, boggy ground.
fact: Cranberry is also the deep red colour of these berries.
fact: «Cranberry sauce» is a sauce made from cranberries, often eaten with turkey.
fact: «Dried cranberries» are cranberries with the water taken out, so they can be kept and eaten as a snack.
fact: Farmers can flood a cranberry bog so the berries float to the top and can be gathered.
exercise: «Grandma spooned cranberry sauce onto her turkey.» What is cranberry sauce? | *A sauce made from sour red berries | A sweet cake with cream | A green apple dip | A gravy made from meat juice
exercise: «Her scarf was a deep cranberry colour.» What colour is cranberry here? | *Deep red | Dark green | Bright yellow | Pale blue
exercise: «The cranberries grew in a wet, boggy field.» Where do cranberries grow? | *In wet, boggy ground | On high, dry mountains | In hot deserts | Under the sea
test: «The farmer flooded the field so the cranberries floated.» What did the farmer do? | He covered the field with snow | *He covered the field with water | He ploughed the field up | He dried the field in the sun
test: «I ate a handful of dried cranberries in my lunchbox.» What are dried cranberries? | *Cranberries with the water taken out, eaten as a snack | Green apples cut into slices | Cranberries cooked into jam for a cake | Fresh berries kept in ice
exam: «The farmer walked across the cranberry bog.» What does cranberry bog mean? | A dry desert | A type of hat | *A wet, boggy field where cranberries grow | A small pond for fish
